# THIS FILE IS COMMITTED ON PURPOSE, and it is the exception to what `.env.example` tells you to do.
#
# Everything Vite reads at build time is baked into the JavaScript bundle, so nothing here can be a secret -
# these four values are already public the moment the app is served. What committing them buys is a build that
# is reproducible from a clean checkout: CI needs no per-environment setup, and a deploy cannot silently ship
# without push notifications or without error reporting because the file was missing from the runner. A value
# that IS a secret (the VAPID private half, the Sentry auth token) is a Worker secret or a CI variable and
# never appears in this directory - see `.dev.vars.example` and `docs/deploy.md`.
#
# These are THIS organisation's identifiers. A fork that deploys its own instance must replace the DSN and the
# VAPID public key with its own, or its error reports and push subscriptions land on ours.
VITE_APP_NAME=HRMS
VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=BOUuKINgFrB579x1TaOA6Ix0leeru-myirthdX1BIqIeUFnvwj0ziqGN6EPVnZp1nq_s6anHE44BtcKLUsgby7I
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=https://b0783df050ada7c6adc0a89aaa15b4f4@o4511976927461376.ingest.de.sentry.io/4511982864498768
VITE_SENTRY_ORG=msphere-io
